# UI Style

## Stack

- shadcn/ui primitives from `@/components/ui/*`
- Tailwind v4 semantic tokens: `bg-background`, `text-muted-foreground`, `border-border`
- Class merge: `cn()` from the project util
- Icons: `lucide-react`
- Toasts: `sonner`
- Themes: `next-themes` (do not invent a parallel theme system)

## Components

- Prefer **named exports** for new components
- Put reusable pieces under `src/components/`; keep page-only UI extractable nearby
- Build on existing `Card`, `Button`, `Badge`, `Input`, dialogs — avoid one-off CSS frameworks

```tsx
// GOOD
import { Card, CardHeader, CardTitle, CardContent } from '@/components/ui/card';
import { cn } from '@/lib/utils';

export function SignalCard({ className, strength }: { className?: string; strength: number }) {
  return (
    <Card className={cn(className)}>
      <CardHeader>
        <CardTitle>Signal</CardTitle>
      </CardHeader>
      <CardContent>{strength} dBm</CardContent>
    </Card>
  );
}
```

## Pages

- Client pages: keep fetch logic in named async functions; explicit loading and error state
- Avoid growing past ~300–500 lines — split charts, tables, and forms into components
- Format rates/bytes/duration via `src/lib/format.ts` when possible
- Do not use `useState<any>`; type API response shapes

## Accessibility and UX

- Buttons and inputs need visible labels or `aria-label`
- Destructive actions confirm when irreversible
- Prefer existing layout patterns (`TopNav`, `PageHeader`) over custom chrome
